{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"c2ba (review-bot shutdown/per-review timeouts unenforceable) is CLOSED — merged to main as 3aec0ae90a with LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 (Gerrit change 1148). The two unbounded residues that made the review-bot stop_grace_period unprovable are now bounded: (1) voter.py offloads the synchronous lock-held emit_code_review_artifact store write off the event loop via asyncio.to_thread, so the drain/per-review wait_for bounds can actually fire; (2) event_append.py routes all 13 lock-held git calls through a new _run_git() bounded by _GIT_TIMEOUT=30 (matching push.py), folding a hung git into a synthetic returncode-124 failure that unwinds cleanly out of write_lock. Defense-in-depth: app.py/config.py bound the lifespan post-drain cancel/await under a new SHUTDOWN_CANCEL_SECONDS (default 10). docker-compose stop_grace_period stays 150s but its comment is re-derived as a provable worst case rather than a risk reduction. This is rec #1's sibling on the write path; the age-ceiling (lock.py) and boot-budget (e43f-area) recs landed earlier this session. Remaining under this hub: e43f (boot-path lock budget), e161 (contention CI flake), 983f (network git call sites, BLOCKED on 01e8)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785559187093068001,"uuid":"e50d8c92-46b6-4d42-96fe-878cb6f82075"}